2,"playId":"401866463340","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3739","guid":"8583e109-c6d2-3606-a402-5af2a5909457","fullName":"Glass Bowl","address":{"city":"Toledo","state":"OH","zipCode":"43606","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3739.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":19137},"article":{"headline":"Long-distance touchdowns spark Toledo in 24-0 win over UMass","description":"— Connor Walendzak scored on a 69-yard touchdown run, Nicholas Thompson returned an interception 62 yards for a touchdown, and Toledo defeated Massachusetts 24-0 on Wednesday night.","story":"TOLEDO, Ohio -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5078063/connor-walendzak\" target=\"_new\">Connor Walendzak</a> scored on a 69-yard touchdown run, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5076049/nicholas-thompson\" target=\"_new\">Nicholas Thompson</a> returned an interception 62 yards for a touchdown, and Toledo defeated Massachusetts 24-0 on Wednesday night.\n\n\r\n              The Rockets (8-2, 5-1) remain in the pack at the top of the Mid-American Conference. Toledo, Western Michigan, Buffalo and Ohio are all 5-1 in the MAC.\n\n\r\n              Walendzak, in his first action this month after being out with an undisclosed injury, capped a 90-yard drive with his long touchdown run, giving Toledo a 7-0 lead late in the first quarter. He finished with 117 yards on 14 carries.\n\n\r\n              Thompson's interception of a <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5298739/logan-inagawa\" target=\"_new\">Logan Inagawa</a> pass made it 17-0 early in the second quarter and Toledo went on to a 24-0 halftime lead that stood up through the second half.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5092811/cj-miller\" target=\"_new\">CJ Miller</a> added 83 yards rushing for the Rockets, who had a total of 239 yards on the ground.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5082330/john-alan-richter\" target=\"_new\">John Alan Richter</a> had 197 yards passing for Toledo.\n\n\r\n              Inagawa completed only 10 of 27 passes for 99 yards but he led the Minutemen (5-5, 2-4) with 40 yards rushing. Starter Pop Watson left after seeming to re-aggravate his ankle, which sidelined him for two games in October.\n\n\r\n              Toledo had a huge advantage in total yards, 436-188. On defense, the Rockets had three sacks and 10 tackles for loss.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              UMass: vs. Akron next Wednesday.\n\n\r\n              Toledo: vs. Bowling Green on Nov. 20. ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-11-12T04:15:34Z"}}